[36mConfigure RHEL 9 to use a FIPS 140-3-compliant systemwide cryptographic policy.[39m

[36mCreate a subpolicy for enhancements to the base systemwide crypto-policy by creating the file /etc/crypto-policies/policies/modules/STIG.pmod with the following content:[39m

[36m# Define ciphers and MACs for OpenSSH and libssh[39m
[36mcipher@SSH=AES-256-GCM AES-256-CTR AES-128-GCM AES-128-CTR[39m
[36mmac@SSH=HMAC-SHA2-512 HMAC-SHA2-256[39m

[36mApply the policy enhancements to the FIPS systemwide cryptographic policy level with the following command:[39m

[36m$ sudo update-crypto-policies --set FIPS:STIG[39m

[36mNote: If additional subpolicies are being employed, they must be added to the update-crypto-policies command.[39m

[36mTo make the cryptographic settings effective for already running services and applications, restart the system:[39m

[36m$ sudo reboot[39m

[36m```[39m
[36mNew:[39m
[36m```[39m
[36mConfigure Amazon Linux 2023 to use a FIPS 140-2/140-3 compliant systemwide cryptographic policy.[39m
[36m [39m
[36mCreate subpolicies for enhancements to the systemwide crypto-policy with the following commands:[39m
[36m [39m
[36mCreate or edit the SCOPES-AND-WILDCARDS policy module in a text editor and insert options that modify the systemwide cryptographic policy as follows:[39m
[36m$ sudo vi /etc/crypto-policies/policies/modules/SCOPES-AND-WILDCARDS.pmod[39m
[36m [39m
[36mAdd the following lines to the policy:[39m
[36m# Disable CHACHA20-POLY1305 for the TLS protocol (OpenSSL, GnuTLS, NSS, and OpenJDK)[39m
[36mcipher@TLS = -CHACHA20-POLY1305[39m
[36m [39m
[36m# Disable all CBC mode ciphers for the SSH protocol (libssh and OpenSSH)[39m
[36mcipher@SSH = -*-CBC[39m
[36m [39m
[36mCreate or edit the OPENSSH-SUBPOLICY module in a text editor and insert options that modify the systemwide crypto-policy as follows:[39m
[36m$ sudo vi /etc/crypto-policies/policies/modules/OPENSSH-SUBPOLICY.pmod[39m
[36m [39m
[36mAdd the following lines to the policy:[39m
[36m# Define ciphers for OpenSSH[39m
[36mcipher@SSH=AES-256-GCM AES-128-GCM AES-256-CTR AES-128-CTR[39m
[36m [39m
[36m# Define MACs for OpenSSH[39m
[36mmac@SSH=HMAC-SHA2-512 HMAC-SHA2-256[39m
[36m [39m
[36mCreate or edit the REQUIRE.pmod file and add the following lines to include the subpolicies in the FIPS configuration with the following command:[39m

[36m$ sudo vi /etc/crypto-policies/policies/modules/REQUIRE.pmod[39m
[36m [39m
[36mAdd the following lines to REQUIRE.pmod:[39m
[36m@OPENSSH-SUBPOLICY[39m
[36m@SCOPES-AND-WILDCARDS[39m
[36m [39m
[36mApply the policy enhancements to the FIPS systemwide cryptographic policy level with the following command:[39m
[36m [39m
[36m$ sudo update-crypto-policies --set FIPS[39m

[36mNote: If additional subpolicies are being employed, they should be added to the REQUIRE.pmod as well. REQUIRE.pmod is included in the systemwide crypto-policy when it is set.[39m
[36m [39m
[36mTo make the cryptographic settings effective for already running services and applications, restart the system:[39m
[36m$ sudo reboot[39m

[36m```[39m
