[36mTerminating network connections associated with communications sessions includes, for example, de-allocating associated TCP/IP address/port pairs at Amazon Linux 2023 level, and de-allocating networking assignments at the application level if multiple application sessions are using a single operating system-level network connection. This does not mean that Amazon Linux 2023 terminates all sessions or network access; it only ends the inactive session and releases the resources associated with that session.[39m



